To print a tuple‑struct’s members by position, treat the `fields` collection as an ordered list and enumerate it. For each element:

```rust
let field_prints = fields.iter.enumerate()
    .map(|(i, f)| {
        if let Some(field_name) = f.ident.as_ref {
            quote!("{}: {:?}", stringify!(#field_name), self.#field_name);
        } else {
            let index = syn::Index::from(i);
            quote!(" .{}: {:?}", #index, self.#index);
        }
    })
    .collect::<Vec<_>>();
```

This code iterates over the comma‑separated fields, checks whether a named field exists (`f.ident`), and if not falls back to the index `i` (converted with `syn::Index`). It then prints each field using its position, which works for any tuple‑struct layout without needing named fields. 

